<title>USA: Koch buys Houston office to expand energy trading.</title>
<headline>Koch buys Houston office to expand energy trading.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Koch Industries Inc has bought a 10-storey, 500,000 square foot office space in Houston to expand its trading operations, Kyle Vann, senior vice president for Crude Oil and Energy Services, said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;We see growth primarily in our trading capabilities - for energy, crude oil, natural gas liquids and chemicals - and in capital services,&quot; Vann said.</p>
<p>Koch currently has about 600 people in Houston and two-thirds of those work for Koch Energy Inc.</p>
<p>Koch Industries is privately held.</p>
<p>((-- David Chance New York Newsroom 212 859 1902))</p>
</text>
